        "record_id": "d43d637b9c5311cd0567076e",
        "score": 0.5951612628958756,
        "section": "isolation",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 179,
        "text": "That means that readers can continue to read the old, original, unaltered content from the original database file at the same time that the writer is appending to the write-ahead log.",
        "title": "isolation"
      },
      {
        "end": 1105,
        "estimated_tokens": 54,
        "kind": "sentence",
        "page_id": 9,
        "position": 8,
        "record_id": "0dc19137b796270a8d2ec298",
        "score": 0.4505397476750449,
        "section": "atomiccommit",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 954,
        "text": "The information in this article applies only when SQLite is operating in \"rollback mode\", or in other words when SQLite is not using a write-ahead log.",
        "title": "atomiccommit"
      },
      {
        "end": 1276,
        "estimated_tokens": 59,
        "kind": "sentence",
        "page_id": 9,
        "position": 9,
        "record_id": "0dc19137b796270a8d2ec298",
        "score": 0.45026196989726713,
        "section": "atomiccommit",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 1105,
        "text": "SQLite still supports atomic commit when write-ahead logging is enabled, but it accomplishes atomic commit by a different mechanism from the one described in this article.",
        "title": "atomiccommit"
      },
      {
        "end": 262,
        "estimated_tokens": 78,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 12,
        "position": 0,
        "record_id": "54295977f935d3e92d41aa5d",
        "score": 0.4493706192154857,
        "section": "pragma",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "If the write-ahead log is enabled (via the journal_mode pragma), this pragma causes a checkpoint operation to run on database database, or on all attached databases if database is omitted. If write-ahead log mode is disabled, this pragma is a harmless no-op.",
        "title": "pragma"
      },
      {
        "end": 501,
        "estimated_tokens": 56,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 11,
        "position": 3,
        "record_id": "86c2f2aecc202302f11dbd80",
        "score": 0.4482238146697657,
        "section": "fileformat2",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 341,
        "text": "During a transaction, SQLite stores additional information in a second file called the \"rollback journal\", or if SQLite is in WAL mode, a write-ahead log file.",
        "title": "fileformat2"
      },
      {
        "end": 1182,
        "estimated_tokens": 79,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 14,
        "position": 5,
        "record_id": "a91aae524418f2c55306061a",
        "score": 0.4053400862599186,
        "section": "wal",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 915,
        "text": "Writers merely append new content to the end of the WAL file. Because writers do nothing that would interfere with the actions of readers, writers and readers can run at the same time. However, since there is only one WAL file, there can only be one writer at a time.",
        "title": "wal"
      },
      {
        "end": 216,
        "estimated_tokens": 66,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 14,
        "position": 0,
        "record_id": "0ae87f7578f62e508e800622",
        "score": 0.39813913850149485,
        "section": "wal",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "The default method by which SQLite implements atomic commit and rollback is a rollback journal. Beginning with version 3.7.0 (2010-07-21), a new \"Write-Ahead Log\" option (hereafter referred to as \"WAL\") is available.",
        "title": "wal"
      },
      {
        "end": 1394,
        "estimated_tokens": 46,
        "kind": "sentence",
        "page_id": 9,
        "position": 10,
        "record_id": "0dc19137b796270a8d2ec298",
        "score": 0.3954892426245398,
        "section": "atomiccommit",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 1276,
        "text": "See the write-ahead log documentation for additional information on how SQLite supports atomic commit in that context.",
        "title": "atomiccommit"
      }
    ],
